  "body": "## What changed\n\n- `assets/posts/tormach-lathe.cps`: `g76Why` refuses the one-block LinuxCNC `G76` when the record's `StartInAir` is not `true`. The check uses the same refusal channel as the other G76 refusals. It runs before the drive-line rapid and the `G76` block, so no block of the cycle is written and the in-app gate writes no file. The cycle words do not change. The text has the form of the Fanuc text of #2878:\n  `G76 threading cycle refused - the start point is above material (G76 moves the insert to pass depth at rapid traverse) - start the thread in free air in front of the end face or in a relief groove wider than the insert, regenerate the operation, or choose G33 passes`\n- The value is the `start_in_air` of PR #2892 (`crates/app/src/operation/g76_start.rs`). The post adds no geometry.\n- `crates/app/tests/tormach_lathe_support/mod.rs`: `thread_world` keeps the solid bar (Z-16 to Z40, start Z14). The new `g76_world` bar runs from Z-26 to its free end face Z14.693, with the top one lead higher (16.3). The cycle starts at Z16 in free air. This is the fixture change of #2892 for Fanuc. Each test that must post a Tormach `G76` now uses `g76_world`.\n- Decision file: `docs/decisions/2952-tormach-g76-start-in-air.md`.\n\n## Readings\n\n- The public LinuxCNC G-code reference, G76 section: with no entry taper, \"the tool will rapid to the cut depth then synchronize and begin the cut\". This post writes no entry taper (no `E` / `L`). Thus each pass moves the insert in at rapid at the start Z.\n- The old golden started at `Z14` on a bar that runs to Z40. That is a rapid into solid material.\n\n## Golden lines that changed\n\nRegenerated only with `WRITE_GOLDEN=1 cargo test -p camcraft-app --test lathe_post_tormach_thread`.\n\n- `golden/nc/tormach-lathe/thread_g76_mm.nc`:\n  - line 12 `G0 Z14` -> `G0 Z16`: the start is now in front of the end face.\n  - line 17 `G0 Z40` removed: the #1604 departure goes +Z only up to the stock face. The new face (Z14.693) is below the Z24 retract, so no move is necessary.\n- `golden/nc/tormach-lathe/thread_g76_inch.nc`: the same two lines (`G0 Z0.5512` -> `G0 Z0.6299`; `G0 Z1.5748` removed).\n- No other golden changed. The G33 goldens are the same.\n\n## Other posts checked for a thread cycle\n\nOnly `fanuc-lathe.cps` (refuses since #2878) and `tormach-lathe.cps` (this PR) write a thread cycle and define `onThreadCycle`. `linuxcnc.cps` `G33.1` is a rigid tap. `tormach.cps`, `grblhal.cps` and `tinyg.cps` refuse `G84`. The other posts have no thread word. The decision file has the table.\n\n## Pins\n\n- New `crates/app/tests/lathe_post_tormach_g76_start.rs`:\n  - `tormach_g76_refuses_by_name_when_the_start_point_is_inside_a_solid_bar` (mm and inch; the gate writes no file)\n  - `tormach_g76_posts_when_the_start_point_is_in_free_air_in_front_of_the_end_face` (mm and inch; posted text asserted, also through the gate)\n  - `tormach_g33_passes_still_post_when_the_start_point_is_inside_a_solid_bar`\n  - `tormach_g76_refuses_a_legacy_stream_without_the_air_word`\n- `a_g76_record_the_cycle_cannot_state_exactly_is_refused_by_name`: 9 cases -> 10 (\"the start point is above material\").\n- `inch_g76_pass_bottoms_match_pathpilot_hub_8l_readings`: the golden line is now `G0 Z0.6299`. The DRO pass bottoms (X and depth) do not change.\n\n## Gate (quick, local, worktree issue-917, `-j 18`, sccache)\n\n- camcraft-app, each binary green: `lathe_post_tormach_thread` 10, `lathe_post_tormach_g76_start` 4, `lathe_post_tormach_g76_ladder` 3, `lathe_post_tormach_g30` 4, `lathe_post_tormach` 8, `lathe_post_g76_start` 5, `lathe_post_g76` 8, `lathe_post_g76_schedule` 7, `lathe_post_inch` 6, `lathe_post_thread_dips` 7, `lathe_post` 7, `conformance` 7, `solid_law_goldens` 7, `program_units` 7, `example_catalog` 29, `example_catalog_edge_work` 1, `catalog_groove_part_off` 1, `lathe_work_spindle` 5, `setup_post_options` 13, `mcp_post_options` 7.\n- `camcraft-post` lib: 78 passed.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-post --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `cargo xtask gate light`: 2 steps, 0 failed.\n- No catalog example uses the Tormach lathe post (`cone-thread` uses Fanuc Lathe).\n- `rustfmt --check`: not a repo gate (no config; files on `main` show the same diffs). Not applied.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- A Tormach start in a relief groove wider than the insert: the Tormach suites have no grooving fixture. The judge is pinned by `g76_start_tests.rs` (`relief_groove_wider_than_insert_passes_when_grooved_and_refuses_when_uncut_or_narrow`).\n- No run on a LinuxCNC or PathPilot control.\n\n## Old projects\n\nA cached record without the value reads false. Its Tormach `G76` is refused by name until the threading operation is regenerated. This is the same rule as the Fanuc post.\n\nChangelog: The Tormach PathPilot lathe post refuses a G76 thread cycle whose start point stands above material (the cycle moves the insert to depth at rapid); start the thread in free air in front of the end face or in a relief groove wider than the insert. Threading operations of older projects must be regenerated before their G76 posts.\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nRefs #2878\nFixes #2952\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
